From: yaoyuping <yaoyuping@hygon.cn>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:57:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 22/24] logits_processor: skinny Triton GEMM for the bf16
 lm_head at M <= 64

hipBLASLt runs the decode lm_head (Step5 shard 32224 x 4096, M = 16/64)
with a 256x256 macro tile at ~0.93 TB/s. A full-M, N-tiled Triton kernel
streams the weight at 1.4-1.7 TB/s: 283 -> 153 us at M=16 and
287 -> 188 us at M=64, i.e. ~0.44 ms per MTP3 step (4 head calls).
bs32 64k/4k decode: 1418.6 -> 1427.6 tok/s (mean of 2 vs 3 runs).

logits_processor.py is outside the torch.compile code hash, so this does
not invalidate compile caches. Disable with STEP5_SKINNY_LM_HEAD=0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
